    "body": "This is another interesting question for @domenic to ponder w.r.t. the Streams API. I'm not sure it is explicitly stated by the specification but for generic streams chunks are atomic, while for byte streams it seems like chunks could be split or merged arbitrarily by the implementation. What are your thoughts here?\r\n\r\nI've added some additional notes on the implementation details to the Chromium issue. I personally think the bootloader is making some sketchy assumptions about how USB serial drivers work but they are assumptions that other APIs don't break.",
