    "updated_at": "2021-02-26T20:16:39Z",
    "body": "I could see us rewriting the write steps so that the underlying sink makes a best-effort attempt to avoid splitting chunks. The only case in which that is inevitable is if the underlying operating system only accepts a partial chunk and we have to retry with the remainder.\r\n\r\nI need to think through the performance and memory usage consequences.",
