    "created_at": "2026-10-01T18:24:05Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-01T18:24:05Z",
    "body": "Current Chromium confirms that a single stream chunk can still be split.\n\n`WriteData()` writes as much of the current `BufferSource` as the Mojo data pipe accepts, increments `offset_`, waits for `MOJO_HANDLE_SIGNAL_WRITABLE`, then continues the same chunk.\n\nSo the practical contract today is not one `writer.write(chunk)` → one OS/USB transaction.\n\nIt may be useful for the spec to say this explicitly even if atomic writes cannot be guaranteed. Otherwise applications can accidentally depend on chunk boundaries that the underlying sink never promised to preserve.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
